is there huge a market for conscious products or am kidding myslef

Short answer:

Yes, there is a huge market.
No, there isn't a huge market for "eco" by itself.

Those are two very different statements.

The market is massive...

Consumers spend hundreds of billions of dollars annually on products that overlap with sustainability:

Outdoor recreation
Travel
Camping
Hiking
Water sports
Organic food
Sustainable fashion
Beauty
Home products
Pet products

Many people prefer environmentally responsible products.

But...

...people rarely buy because it's eco-friendly.

They buy because it is:

Better
Safer
Healthier
More durable
More beautiful
Higher performance
More convenient

The eco aspect is often the bonus.

For example:

❌ "This sunscreen is reef safe."

Nice.

✅ "This sunscreen lasts 8 hours, doesn't sting your eyes while snorkeling, and is reef safe."

Much stronger.

Think of Patagonia

People don't buy Patagonia because they're saving the planet.

They buy because

excellent quality
lifetime warranty
great design
trusted brand

The environmental mission strengthens the brand.

It isn't usually the first reason.

Think of YETI

A cooler for CAD $500.

People don't buy it because of sustainability.

They buy because

keeps ice for days
durable
premium
